<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amalaberga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amalaberga was a niece of the Ostrogothic king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoric-the-great">Theodoric the Great</a>, the daughter of his sister Amalafrida. Around 510 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herminafrid">Herminafrid</a>, king of the Thuringians, linking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> to Theodoric's alliance system. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> destroyed the Thuringian kingdom in 531 she fled with her children to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p></div>
